#
# Included by default_sailfish.pa.d/droid.pa instead of its default
# "load-module module-droid-card rate=48000".
#
# The primary module that module-droid-card opens is audio.hidl_compat (through
# the symlink /usr/libexec/droid-hybris/system/lib64/hw/audio.primary.parrot.so),
# which forwards to the vendor's HIDL audio service. Volume is applied in
# PulseAudio, as on the other hidl_compat ports.
#
# config=: pulseaudio-modules-droid looks for audio_policy_configuration.xml
# only in /odm/etc, /vendor/etc/audio, /vendor/etc and /system/etc
# (src/common/droid-config.c). pdx246's vendor keeps it per SKU, in
# /vendor/etc/audio/sku_parrot/ (its xi:include paths are absolute); without
# this the card did not load ("Failed to parse any configuration", fifth boot).
#
# unload_call_exit=true: at stop, exit(0) when the hw module is released instead
# of closing it. Unloading module-droid-card unmaps libhybris-common, and the
# static destructors of Android libraries that exit() runs afterwards
# (libmediautils' TimerThread) still call its pthread hooks: PulseAudio
# segfaulted at every stop (2026-10-30). Takes effect with the hw module
# reference fix in pulseaudio-modules-droid (branch pdx246-14.2.110); without
# it the module was never released and PulseAudio aborted in core_free().
load-module module-droid-card rate=48000 hw_volume=false config=/vendor/etc/audio/sku_parrot/audio_policy_configuration.xml unload_call_exit=true
